# Reproducible builds: the companion asset pipeline hashes working-tree bytes
# (scripts/build-companion-assets.mjs), so every text file must check out with
# the same bytes on every machine. The index is already 100% LF; this pins the
# checkout direction that core.autocrlf=true would otherwise vary per-machine.
# These attributes only apply when git writes a file, so a checkout made
# before they landed keeps its old endings and git status stays clean about it.
# npm run check:eol-hygiene reports that drift; --fix re-checks-out the files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one consumer that prefers CRLF on disk.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Media assets are binary.
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.png binary
